$ wavesleuth-devito simulate --help

usage: wavesleuth-devito simulate [-h] --out OUT [--quiet] [--no-wavefield]
                                  [--shot-mode {simultaneous,sequential}]
                                  [--boundary {none,sponge}]
                                  [--sponge-width SPONGE_WIDTH]
                                  [--sponge-strength SPONGE_STRENGTH]
                                  [--noise-level NOISE_LEVEL]
                                  [--receiver-dropout RECEIVER_DROPOUT]
                                  [--amplitude-jitter AMPLITUDE_JITTER]
                                  [--time-jitter TIME_JITTER]
                                  [--noise-seed NOISE_SEED]
                                  world

positional arguments:
  world                 Input world JSON path.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --out OUT             Output run .npz path.
  --quiet               Reduce Devito logging.
  --no-wavefield        Do not save final wavefield/snapshots.
  --shot-mode {simultaneous,sequential}
  --boundary {none,sponge}
  --sponge-width SPONGE_WIDTH
  --sponge-strength SPONGE_STRENGTH
  --noise-level NOISE_LEVEL
                        Add Gaussian noise relative to trace RMS.
  --receiver-dropout RECEIVER_DROPOUT
                        Randomly zero a fraction of receiver channels.
  --amplitude-jitter AMPLITUDE_JITTER
                        Per-channel amplitude gain jitter.
  --time-jitter TIME_JITTER
                        Per-channel timing jitter in seconds.
  --noise-seed NOISE_SEED
